{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"18ada617-a313-4276-a667-6a30b7bab907","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Root Cause\n\nIn Flutter (`posthog_flutter`), session replay captures screenshots of the widget tree via `PostHogWidget`. Without `PostHogWidget` wrapping the root app widget, custom events ([`Analytics.track`](file:///tmp/h-kjioJa/lib/analytics.dart#L14-L15)), lifecycle events, and router screen transitions (`PosthogObserver`) still arrive in PostHog without errors, but no frames are captured for replay.\n\n- [`LegacyApp`](file:///tmp/h-kjioJa/lib/legacy_app.dart#L8-L25) wraps its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`, so session replay worked for the old UI A/B group (`NEW_UI=false`).\n- [`NewApp`](file:///tmp/h-kjioJa/lib/new_app.dart#L19-L36) returned `MaterialApp.router` directly without wrapping it in `PostHogWidget`, leaving replays empty for users on the new UI (`NEW_UI=true`).\n\n### Fix \u0026 Notes\n\n- Wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` (with an explanatory comment) in [`NewApp.build`](file:///tmp/h-kjioJa/lib/new_app.dart#L22-L35).\n- Added the full explanation and breakdown of which parts of the colleague's note applied vs. were already configured in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-kjioJa/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":117.278392,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":38022,"output_tokens":7212,"thinking_tokens":4393,"cache_read_tokens":163606,"total_tokens":45234}}}
